Changelog: 04-11-2026 21:04:23

Version 0.2.0.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 20:53:37

Added. The Dev app versions tile (owner, 04-11-2026): the Nexus apps with their versions, what changed since each
one's last version and the version that asks for, set with Set version (the checkout's tools/dev_versions.py),
another one typed or with a note.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 20:28:29

Added. A click on Nexus's icon in the header opens the Nexus page (owner, 04-11-2026). What this app does no longer
calls Nexus Demo Recorder Linux only.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 20:08:16

Added. The Nexus Demo Recorder tile is on on Windows too: the recorder runs there (its run.ps1). A Nexus app's tile
is now off only where the app has no run script for this system, and its tooltip says so.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 19:48:43

Fixed. run.sh starts Nexus Dashboard from Git Bash on Windows too: it looked only for the Linux venv, and now takes
.venv-windows there, as Nexus Release Tool's run.sh does.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 19:05:17

Fixed. On Windows the Portal video tour and Apps video tour of a Windows suite only said "Could not start": the
dialogs started the suite's script with setsid, which Windows does not have. There they start it with bash (Git
Bash) directly, and Stop ends the script and what it started with taskkill /T. The tests no longer expect Linux
paths on Windows, and expect the Installer Tests and Sound Lab tiles on there.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 15:05:00

Fixed. On Windows a click on Nexus Release Tool or Nexus Sound Lab started nothing: the dashboard started
run.ps1 with PowerShell as a detached process, and PowerShell without a console quits at once with code 0
without running the script, so the log stayed empty. It now starts without a console window, in a process
group of its own, and keeps running when the dashboard closes; a test runs a run.ps1 through it.

Changelog: 04-11-2026 10:54:41

Added. Test local apps and Close issues, from Nexus Release Tool's Test on this board (owner, 04-11-2026: the
release tool is the release, the dashboard the place for working on a suite). Under the tiles, Test local apps
shows the chosen suite's portal and app windows from the checkout (an orange ! on an app that changes the board,
which asks first; an open portal is warned about, not started again) and the suite's wiki and the Nexus page served
with mkdocs serve (Wikis on the network serves them for the other devices too); a click starts one with the dev
venv and the checkout's core, its log in ~/.cache/nexus-dashboard/local/, the end of it shown when it stops with an
error. The Close issues tile lists the open GitHub issues and closes the ticked ones with gh issue close, one after
the other, its output in the window (it ran in the release tool's Commands tab). The tiles keep two rows; the
window is 900 by 820. The code is local.py and issues.py, moved from the release tool's plan.py, with their tests.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 02:11:57

Added. The About text names Nexus Sound Lab (dev/sounds) among the Nexus apps the tiles start; the tiles found it
by themselves.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 00:56:43

Added. Nexus Dashboard, a Nexus app in dev/dash/ (owner, 02-11-2026: the tools for working on the suites were
spread over the suites and the root; one door to them, with the tools kept where their suite's rules put them).
The window: the suite chosen in the header (remembered; --suite NAME opens one), tiles for the Nexus apps of the
checkout (Nexus Release Tool, Nexus Demo Recorder, Nexus Installer Tests: a click starts the app with its run
script in a window of its own, with the suite where the app takes one, and says where its log is), then the
suite's tools as dialogs: Portal video tour and Apps video tour (from the Media Tool, on the suite's record-tour.sh
and record-app-tour.sh, with the size 1080p, 1440p or 2160p) and Convert icons (tools/sync_icons.py on the suite).
A tile is greyed out where it does not run here: the Demo Recorder on Windows, a suite's tours on the other
system, the icons for a suite whose apps take no category icons. It runs from the checkout with the dev venv
(run.sh, run.ps1), takes Nexus's design and icon (core's nexus.py), and is never released (.checkout-only).
install.sh and install.ps1 write the launcher, the menu entry and the Desktop icon for this checkout.
